 "stimulus_html": "<p>For questions 4 – 6, use the three graphs below:</p>\n<blockquote>\n  <p>The three graphs represent the progress of three runners in a 400-meter race.<br> The solid line represents Runner A. The dotted line represents Runner B. The dashed line represents Runner C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><img src=\"exercises/media/43b98fadfcacf582.svg\" alt=\"A graph showing PROBLEM POPULATION on the y-axis (k=0-3) versus INITIAL POPULATION on the x-axis (i=0-5). Three lines - solid, dashed, and dotted - depict different downward trends from top-left to bottom-right.\"></p>",
